Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.980
Say hi to Youtube!

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:03.980
"Hi Youtube!"

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:08.100
*keyboard typing*

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:12.960
Hey everyone! What's happening? I'm sorry I've been a little MIA (missing in action) recently

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:18.820
I got sick last week and my parents visiting and work was really busy but I am back in full force.

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:20.700
#FULLFORCE

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:24.500
Today I wanted to answer a common question that I've gotten from so many of you.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:27.580
Do you need to be good at math to be a Software Engineer?

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:33.260
The overall answer that I've been giving to everyone and I'm just gonna tell you right now is

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:37.020
NO you don't have to be great at math to be a software engineer.

00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:39.720
But you do have to be able to reason logically.

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:42.480
"Okay Mayuko but what do you mean by that?"

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:46.280
Well other Mayuko, I am going to dive into that today.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:50.760
I want to note that I am a mobile engineer and have been for my whole career

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:54.920
and so I don't have very much expertise in the other areas of software engineering

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:57.900
and so I'm going to try my best to talk about them

00:00:57.980 --> 00:01:03.080
If you are in these other areas of software engineering, I would love for you to leave a comment down below

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:05.540
explaining how you use math in your jobs.

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:07.260
So let's jump in!

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:12.360
First of all, there are several different kinds of software engineering jobs out there

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:13.840
You could be a:

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:21.100
Mobile engineer, infrastructure engineer, game engineer, frontend engineer, backend data engineer

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:26.480
Well this list isn't exhaustive, I would say these are the most common types of software engineering jobs

00:01:26.481 --> 00:01:32.340
and all of these require different technologies and different areas of expertise in software engineering

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:39.520
and it's because of this diversity in software engineering jobs that you can be working on some really math heavy stuff or not at all

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:47.040
Game engineers to my knowledge use a lot of math in their jobs as they use code to model the laws of Physics in their games.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:51.680
For instance writing code for how gravity works when a player jumps up and down

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:55.280
or how light should reflect on the character from different angles

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:58.740
In contrast, I write apps that require very little math.

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:02.700
The code involved is usually making an app out of parts that Apple provides.

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:07.920
And usually taking data from a database and showing them in a user-friendly manner in an app.

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:13.140
One thing however, that is common to all areas of software engineering in terms of math

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:15.140
is the ability to reason logically.

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:22.300
Code is just a series of logical statements and so logical reasoning is really important for reading, writing and fixing code.

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:30.300
So while math could be important to a software engineering job, it usually plays an integral part in computer science related degrees

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:37.300
Most universities require college-level math classes as a prerequisite to take more advanced computer science classes

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:40.380
At my school I remember needing to take Calculus,

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:44.980
Differential Equations, Linear Algebra and Probability and Statistics

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:51.680
Also, some computer science classes are more math heavy than others and some require needing to do

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:53.920
bit-wise calculations and for others— vector calculus.

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:59.560
But it makes sense that they require these things because a computer science degree is set up

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:02.240
so that you could go into any field of software engineering.

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:06.800
Although I don't use most of the math-y topics that i learned in college

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:08.740
they did serve as a very strong foundation

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:12.840
for me to get into any software engineering career that I was passionate about.

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:20.000
So to sum this all up, most universities will require a decent amount of college-level mathematics courses

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:26.060
and math knowledge for CS classes but depending on which software engineering career you choose,

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:32.260
a strong foundation in Math could be really important to your day to day job but it also could not be.

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:36.320
The most important thing to remember though is that logical reasoning is

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:40.810
probably the most important math related skill for any software engineering job.

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:46.280
Again if you have had any different experiences from my own

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:49.880
Please leave a comment down below and let us know what your experience has been

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:54.498
Cool! That's it and thank you so much for watching. I hope you enjoyed this video.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:57.120
I know that math can be kind of a scary topic

00:03:57.120 --> 00:04:01.140
and especially if you want to go into software engineering, it can be kind of the big wall

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:04.160
but I hope this inspired you.

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:10.100
With that said thank you so much to everyone who has liked, commented and shared my video

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:11.480
and also sent me a message

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:16.720
you all continue to be my biggest motivator in the scary new adventure called YouTube

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:23.940
